  "description": "RAW SRAM\n\nAn engaging and sprited ride for folks venturing beyond gravel.\n\n- Bikepacking.com\n\nEvery MASON bicycle is built for adventures. But the RAW is the bicycle created for the biggest, roughest, most off-the-grid journeys on the planet.\n\nWith its flat bar layout and 120mm suspension fork, the RAW takes a mountain bike format and pushes it further: into the realms of bikepacking, adventure racing and remote exploration. Multiple equipment-mounting points enable the longest voyages, carrying fluids, food, and camping gear for the long haul, without compromising on serious off-road performance. Combining a custom mix of Dedacciai and Reynolds tubing, the RAW is built by hand in Scotland to exacting specifications. The latest update for 2025 future-proofs the RAW with MASON-designed UDH (Universal Derailleur Hanger) dropouts – designed carefully to open up a full choice of modern transmission specifications. Other updates include dedicated rack-mount eyelets at the base of the seat stays and a new colour choice: AccursedOchre.\n\nThe RAW is race-proven, with a record that includes the Atlas Mountain Race, the Silk Road Mountain Race and the Highland Trail 550. Race after race, it has delivered results for ultra racers taking on the biggest terrain with days’ or weeks’ worth of kit.\n\nSRAM's groupset options for the RAW bring together features like a 520% gear range and fully customisable wireless shifting. New for 2025, the addition of the Universal Derailleur Hanger standard enables SRAM's direct-mount Transmission derailleur, with its unrivalled accuracy and ease of set-up.\n\nOur recommended fork is the Rockshox SID Ultimate. Well balanced to cater for trail riding with 120mm travel and a 44mm offset, the SID Ultimate is packed in a stiff, lightweight 35mm chassis, and is equipped with the top of the line Charger Race Day damper and bolt-on arch mounted mudguard.\n\nFinishing off the build, a Hunt Trailwide V2 wheelset provides optimal toughness and ride quality, while other options are available too.\n\nChoice of Schwalbe, Maxxis or Vittoria 29” tyres in various widths and tread patterns\n\nPowerful and adjustable SRAM G2 RSC hydrualic brakes.\n\nSRAM GX AXS Wireless Groupset\n\nPNW Loam 31.6 dropper post.\n\nEyebolts can be fitted for rack mounting on dropouts, or removed and replaced with a stainless grub screw for a clean aesthetic.\n\nMASON ‘Element’ 3D printed TPU chainstay protector.\n\nPremium quality ‘black stainless’ bolt and fittings set.\n\nProvisions for bolt-on top tube bag and ample full frame bag space with with opened-out front triangle.\n\nRockshox SID Ultimate fork, with 120mm travel and 44mm offset\n\nFabrication and wet-painting by Scottish-based Five Land Bikes, as well as eCoat corrosion treatment inside and out.",
